        {
          "path": "_m/u/1/2/b/ipswich-museum-wp/james-conder-token.jpg",
          "filename": "James Conder token.jpg",
          "caption": "James Conder was the first to catalog the late 18th Century British Provincial coinage.  Today, such unofficial tokens are called 'Conder Tokens.'\nGenuine small change was not being produced by the government, per King George III, and leave was granted for privately struck tokens to circulate.  It was the height of the Industrial Revolution, and they had suddenly developed the steam engine and the steam coin press, had built the first iron bridge, and an iron ship, apparently a sailing barge. People were moving from barter to use of currency, and it was badly needed.\nThis token advertised Mr. Conder's drapery shop, and he was an avid coin collector.\n\nThis is a very gratifying find, found on ebay, and which arrived recently.",
          "alt": "James Conder was the first to catalog the late 18th Century British Provincial coinage.  Today, such unofficial tokens are called 'Conder Tokens.'\nGenuine small change was not being produced by the government, per King George III, and leave was granted for privately struck tokens to circulate.  It was the height of the Industrial Revolution, and they had suddenly developed the steam engine and the steam coin press, had built the first iron bridge, and an iron ship, apparently a sailing barge. People were moving from barter to use of currency, and it was badly needed.\nThis token advertised Mr. Conder's drapery shop, and he was an avid coin collector.\n\nThis is a very gratifying find, found on ebay, and which arrived recently.",
          "width": 1704,
          "height": 845,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "Larry Moran from Chicago, United States",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:James_Conder_token.jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "ipswich-museum-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "u12b",
          "categories": [
            "CC-BY-2.0",
            "Conder tokens",
            "Ipswich Museum"
          ],
          "smallPath": "_m/u/1/2/b/ipswich-museum-wp/james-conder-token-small.webp"
